course: dictionary
lesson: 15105
title: Words that break
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe things that burst open suddenly, and rupture is one of them. Read the words around it to find its meaning: «The old water pipe ruptured in the night, and the kitchen floor was soon full of water.» A pipe that bursts open lets water pour out, so ruptured means burst or broken open.
explain: Rupture can also be a noun, meaning a burst or a break. «The doctor said the rupture needed an operation straight away.» A break inside the body is serious, so the clues tell you it means a break that needs help quickly.
explain: A rupture can also be a break in people's feelings or promises. «After the lie, their friendship ruptured and they stopped speaking.» A friendship cannot burst like a pipe, so ask what would fit here. A sudden break is the meaning that makes sense.
fact: Rupture means to burst or break open suddenly.
fact: A rupture is a burst or a break.
fact: «A ruptured pipe» is a pipe that has burst open and may leak.
fact: «Ruptured appendix» is an emergency, so a doctor must help quickly.
fact: In an earthquake, the Earth's crust can rupture, which means the ground cracks open.
exercise: «The old pipe ruptured under the sink.» What does ruptured mean? | *Burst open | Painted bright blue | Carefully mended | Frozen solid
exercise: «The earthquake made the ground rupture.» What is happening to the ground? | It goes soft and sandy | It turns into a lake | *It cracks open | It rises into a hill
exercise: «The ruptured hose sprayed water everywhere.» Which word tells you the hose had burst open? | everywhere | sprayed | *ruptured | hose
test: «The doctor said his ruptured appendix was an emergency.» What does this mean? | *A break inside that needs help straight away | Something funny he ate | A sore throat | A tiny scratch that will heal alone
test: «After the lie, their friendship had a rupture and they stopped talking.» What does rupture mean here? | A new game | *A sudden break | A long, happy holiday | A gentle hug
exam: Ella says a rupture is always about pipes. Is she right? | Yes, but only in the kitchen | Yes, only pipes can rupture | *No, a rupture can also be a break in a friendship or agreement | No, it means a happy surprise
